          {
            "typeName": "notesText",
            "multiple": false,
            "typeClass": "primitive",
            "value": "Project: Mood and Movement in Daily life.\r\nThe primary aim of this study is to investigate the role of physical activity in the etiology of depressed mood, individual differences therein, and clues for tailor-made interventions. A second aim of this study is to elucidate the temporal relationship between mood symptoms and several stress-related hormones and enzymes, such as cortisol and alpha-amylase."
